What is Color Gamut?
{sentence}
Color gamut is defined as the range of colors which a particular device can produce or record.
{sentence}
It is usually shown by an enclosed area of the primary colors of the device on the chromaticity diagram.
{sentence}
For example, the primary colors of monitors are red, green, and blue. Hence, the color gamut of a monitor is shown in a triangular area enclosed by the color coordinates of the monitor's red, green, and blue colors.
{sentence}
